---
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>What you will do</h2>
  <p>
    Six times this semester you give or receive a note --- written feedback
    on a specific piece of work, in a different domain each time: a drawing,
    a pull request, a paragraph, a proposal under blind review, a restaurant,
    and the brief that assigned all of it. The rest of the weeks apply,
    revise or turn the same method on itself.
    The domain changes; the method doesn't. By week 12 you'll have a
    portfolio of notes across six domains and a clear answer to whether the
    method actually travels, because you'll have tested it yourself, in the
    room,
    on work that mattered to whoever made it.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone who has to give feedback on someone else's work and has noticed
    that most of what passes for feedback is a reaction with a compliment
    sandwiched around it. There's no studio-art or software prerequisite ---
    the crits rotate across enough domains that no single background gives
    you an advantage for more than a fortnight. What it does assume is that
    you're willing to write a claim specific enough that someone could prove
    you wrong, and sit in a room while they try.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>The weekly schedule: what domain, what's due, what you bring.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>What is marked, what it is worth, and when it is due.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who teaches the course and how to reach them.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Policies" href="/policies/">
      <p>Attendance, late work, and what a note is not allowed to be.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
